    <div>

        <section id="bs"
            class="game-card rounded-3xl overflow-hidden bg-[#562447] border border-[var(--sayori-border)]">
            <header class="card-header px-8 py-12">
                <div class="card-symbol">
                    💥
                </div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--sayori-lavender-bright)]">Battleship</h2>
                <p class="card-tagline">
                    My favourite game from this section. it is game requiring strategy and decision making skills.
                </p>
            </header>

            <div class="px-8 pb-8 space-y-10">
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        🎮 How to Play
                    </h3>

                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-8">
                        This game is played in the dm. No matter which channel you start.
                        Both players secretly place their ships on the board by typing <code>attack &lt;cordinate_number&gt;</code>. During each turn,
                        choose a coordinate to fire at using <code>attack &lt;co-ordinate_number&gt;</code>. A hit damages your opponent's fleet,
                        while a miss simply ends your turn, because why not? Sink every enemy ship before yours are destroyed to win the battle.
                    </p>

                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>- Ships are hidden from your opponent.</li>
                        <li>- Every turn you may attack one coordinate.</li>
                        <li>- A successful hit reveals part of an enemy ship.</li>
                        <li>- Sink every ship to win the match.</li>
                        <li>- In the embed you can see the coordinates which you attacked on.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        ⌨ Commands
                    </h3>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="!battleship">
                            !battleship
                        </button>
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="rotate">
                            rotate
                        </button>
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="place">
                            place
                        </button>
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="attack">
                            attack
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold"> Tips </h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>- Spread your shots instead of attacking random nearby tiles.</li>
                        <li>- Once you find part of a ship, check the surrounding tiles to locate the rest.</li>
                        <li>- Since majority part of the game take place in Sayori's dms, you do not need to write the prefix before rotate, attack or place.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold"> How I play this! </h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>- So, I try to figure out where and how I should place my fleet to make sure that opponent will literally have to cover 50% of the board before reaching my last ship.</li>
                        <li>- Once I am ready, I wait for the opponent and then the game start.</li>
                        <li>- I pick a random coordinate on left side, preferrably from first 3 columns. Then no matter hit or miss, I move toward left leaving three columns.
                            <ul>
                                <li>for example, I started with <code>attack d3</code>, my next move will be <code>attack d7</code></li>
                                <li>Notice, there is 3 columns skipped.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>A lot of time, you need to improvise your strategy midgame. A strategy works against one opponent but it doesn't guarantee then it can help you win against others as well.</li>
                        <li>Best of luck.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
        </section>
        <div class="min-h-[3px]"></div>
        <section id="cf"
            class="game-card rounded-3xl overflow-hidden bg-[#562447] border border-[var(--sayori-border)]">
            <header class="card-header px-8 py-12">
                <div class="card-symbol">
                    💥
                </div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--sayori-lavender-bright)]">Connect4</h2>
                <p class="card-tagline">
                    A good 2 player game with few lines and red and yellow dics.
                </p>
            </header>

            <div class="px-8 pb-8 space-y-10">
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        🎮 How to Play
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-8">
                        Drop your coloured disc into one of the columns. The first player to connect
                        four discs in a row wins. The line can be horizontal, vertical or diagonal. See, direction of
                        line doesn't matter as long as it is straight.
                    </p>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        ⌨ Commands
                    </h3>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="/connectfour">
                            /connectfour
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold">
                        Tips
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>- Control the centre columns as much possible. Trust me bro.</li>
                        <li>- Don't only look for your own win, block your opponent too. Because you are watching
                            opportunity, the opponent is too.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
        </section>
        <div class="min-h-[3px]"></div>
        <section id="rps"
            class="game-card rounded-3xl overflow-hidden bg-[#562447] border border-[var(--sayori-border)]">
            <header class="card-header px-8 py-12">
                <div class="card-symbol">
                    📜
                </div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--sayori-lavender-bright)]">Rock Paper Scissor</h2>
                <p class="card-tagline">
                    Who doesn't know this game? Rock Paper Scissor shoot, and boom!
                </p>
            </header>

            <div class="px-8 pb-8 space-y-10">
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        🎮 How to Play
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-8">
                        Both players secretly choose Rock, Paper or Scissors. Once both have made
                        their choice, Sayori reveals the result and declares the winner.
                        <br>
                        More details?
                        Come on man, I don't get paid enough to write a guide on 'how to play rps?', isn't it a common knowledge?
                    </p>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        ⌨ Commands
                    </h3>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="/rps">
                            /rps
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold">
                        Things I assume you already know, but sie we are here, here's a quick reminder:
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>- Rock beats Scissors.</li>
                        <li>- Scissors beats Paper.</li>
                        <li>- Paper beats Rock.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
        </section>
        <div class="min-h-[3px]"></div>
        <section id="ttt"
            class="game-card rounded-3xl overflow-hidden bg-[#562447] border border-[var(--sayori-border)]">
            <header class="card-header px-8 py-12">
                <div class="card-symbol">
                    ⭕
                </div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--sayori-lavender-bright)]">Tictactoe</h2>
                <p class="card-tagline">
                    Really? This game is stupid. Like there is no way to win this damn game. It always ends in a tie. What kind of game always ends in a tie?
                    <br>
                    Wait wait, you actually won the game against someone? Damn, you smartie pants.
                </p>
            </header>
            <div class="px-8 pb-8 space-y-10">
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        🎮 How to Play
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-8">
                        Take turns placing your mark on the board. The first player to connect
                        three marks in a row wins.
                    </p>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        ⌨ Commands
                    </h3>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="/tictactoe">
                            /tictactoe
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold">
                        Tips
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>- The centre tile is usually the strongest opening move.</li>
                        <li>- Always look one move ahead before placing your mark.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
        </section>
        <div class="min-h-[3px]"></div>
        <section id="wordlec"
            class="game-card rounded-3xl overflow-hidden bg-[#562447] border border-[var(--sayori-border)]">
            <header class="card-header px-8 py-12">
                <div class="card-symbol">
                    🔠
                </div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--sayori-lavender-bright)]">Wordle Challenge</h2>
                <p class="card-tagline">
                    Too pro for wordle!
